@startuml TestingLayer4Sequence
' SPEC source: e2e/e2e_test.go
' Layer 4 — the promptful flow over time: drive -> prompt -> model -> side effect.
' Build tag: //go:build e2e; no env gate — preconditions_test.go skips on missing infra
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam shadowing false

' purpose: the promptful Layer-4 flow over time — drive, prompt, model, side effect
' covers: e2e/e2e_test.go
' covers: internal/tmux/**
'
' The topology, the posture flags and the workspace .env rule are in
' 40-agent-e2e-components.puml; the shared instrumentation and skip rules are in
' testing-strategy.puml.
'
' The prompt is not typed. Everything after `--` is forwarded to the agent, so
' `opencode run --auto --agent build <task>` takes the task from argv — one
' deterministic shell command — and exits. tmux exists only to supply the PTY that
' `docker run -it` requires, which is why there is no TUI readiness race here.
'
' Three side effects are polled TOGETHER, host-side, on a 4-minute deadline at
' 3-second intervals: FROM_SAMPLE.txt (the mounted README's first line, proving the
' mount), DONE.txt (the marker BANANA-E2E-OK, proving a write), and SCRAPED.html
' (example.com's stable title "Example Domain", proving egress). Waiting on the
' marker alone would let a broken mount or a blocked egress pass.
'
' ── THE SAMPLE IS COMMITTED, NOT MERELY INITIALISED ────────────────────────
' (the same rule testing-strategy.puml states for probes: sbx clones COMMITTED
'  history, so an untracked file never crosses into the sandbox)
' The lane used to `git init` the copied sample and stop there. A CLONE carries
' COMMITS, so under sbx's default clone the agent opened a workspace whose files
' were untracked and absent: `head -1 README.md` had nothing to read, and the
' first assertion failed on an empty FROM_SAMPLE.txt while the agent had done
' everything it was asked. The lane now `git add -A` and commits with its own
' identity flags — a repo with no user.email cannot commit, and setting one
' globally on a developer host is not the suite's to do.
'
' ── THE THREE READS GO THROUGH ONE ACCESSOR ────────────────────────────────
' Each side effect is read by `delivered`, which answers from the mounted
' workspace when there is one and otherwise from the refs teardown fetched —
' trying both the bare path and `reports/<path>`, because a cloned run lifts the
' agent's output directory there (_spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml).
'
' ── AND THE RUN ENDING IS NOT THE ANSWER ARRIVING ──────────────────────────
' When the tmux session is gone the poll does not conclude: a cloned workspace
' delivers at TEARDOWN, so the lane keeps asking for a bounded settle window
' (PROVEO_TEST_TEARDOWN_TIMEOUT, default 2 minutes), re-reads all three, and only
' then fails — printing the refs it did find, so "incomplete" says whether the
' agent wrote nothing or wrote where nothing looked.

title Layer 4 · Agent E2E — promptful flow (-tags=e2e; assert the side effect)

actor "E2E test / CI" as Test
participant "tmux (internal/tmux)" as Tmux
participant "harness TUI (docker run -it)" as Harness
participant "Ollama sidecar" as Ollama
database "output mount" as FS

Test -> Tmux : Start(proveo run <target> --local-model gemma4)
Tmux -> Harness : launch in headless PTY
note over Ollama : sidecar starts;\nmodel cold-loads on first call
Harness --> Tmux : prints ready prompt
Test -> Tmux : WaitFor("ready")
Tmux --> Test : matched

Test -> Tmux : SendText(task prompt) + Enter
Tmux -> Harness : keystrokes -> stdin
Harness -> Ollama : POST /v1/chat/completions (NO_PROXY)
note right of Ollama : cold-load can take minutes\n(wait-for-serving + long timeout)
Ollama --> Harness : reply (may include reasoning preamble)
Harness -> FS : curl → SCRAPED.html · head -1 README.md → FROM_SAMPLE.txt\nprintf BANANA-E2E-OK → DONE.txt

loop poll all three every 3s, deadline 4m
  Test -> FS : read DONE.txt · FROM_SAMPLE.txt · SCRAPED.html
end
Test -> Test : assert marker + README first line + 'Example Domain'
Test -> Tmux : Kill (+ egress teardown)

note over Test, FS
Assert the **side effect** (DONE.txt), never the transcript — the model's prose
is non-deterministic. Poll with timeout; never a fixed sleep.
end note

note over Test, FS
  **A clone carries commits, so the sample is
  committed.** An initialised but uncommitted
  workspace reaches the agent with no files
  present, and the mount assertion then fails on
  a run that did everything it was asked.
end note

note over Test, FS
  **The run ending is not the answer arriving.**
  A cloned workspace delivers at teardown, so a
  dead session starts a bounded settle window
  instead of a verdict, and the failure prints
  the refs it found beside what it wanted.
end note
@enduml
